{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat assignments/T-K-handoff-observe-archive.md'","aggregated_output":"# Assignment T-K (parent: campaign c1 / W5; orchestrator = Claude) — follow-up to T-E\nProblem found by integration (decisions to cite: experiments/handoff-real/): cc/engine_handoff/engine_handoff.py treats everything in build-record.json as a *declared* claim and only copies *observed* facts, so `generate` leaves release.expected_image_config_id, release.executable_sha256 and release.platform null, and `validate` rejects a genuinely good delivery. The real Build CC record (builds/results/b0-baseline-3/build-record.json; schema_version 1, nested: image.Id, archive.{sha256,bytes}, tools{\"/app/<tool>\": sha}, platform, source.commit, base_images) is now normalized by normalize_build_record() (already added). The remaining step is to OBSERVE these facts from the archive itself instead of trusting the record.\nTasks (edit only cc/engine_handoff/ ; keep existing 48 tests passing; add tests):\n1. Add `observe_archive(path)` to engine_handoff.py: stream-read the `docker save` tarball (real example: /home/muk/projects/siminfeng/campaign/builds/results/b0-baseline-3/engine-image.docker.tar, 2.2 GB, 23-ish blobs; support both classic manifest.json layout and OCI index.json/blobs layout; DO NOT extract to disk wholesale; stream layers, gz or plain). Return: image_config_id (digest of the config blob = Docker image ID, verify the blob's own sha256 matches its name), platform (\"linux/amd64\" from config os/architecture), layer_count, and executables: for each regular file under app/ in the merged layer view (later layers override earlier; honour whiteouts minimally) its sha256 (stream-hash; only for paths under app/ with executable bit). Keep memory bounded.\n2. In collect_facts: add these as OBSERVED facts (source = archive path) and cross-check them against the build-record claims (normalized): mismatch => an `unresolved`/discrepancy entry, never silently pick one. `generate` must then fill release.expected_image_config_id, release.platform and release.executable_sha256 from OBSERVED values only. `validate` must additionally re-observe the archive when it is locally readable and reject if the handoff's identities differ from the re-observed ones (tamper: modify one byte in a layer blob => rejected with a precise reason; this must also hold when sha256/bytes in the handoff are still those of the original file because someone edited only the handoff).\n3. Add `generate --requirements FILE.yaml`: a requester-declared file with handoff_id, release.role, inputs.model.{repository,revision,manifest,manifest_sha256}, inputs.workload (artifact path+sha computed), sandbox_requirements.{gpu{vendor,count}, required_runtime_compatibility, resource_limits{cpus,memory,pids,timeout_s}, network_after_staging}, tests.{requested,policy_reference,profiling{requested,tool_and_version}}. Values from this file are tagged `declared` in facts/handoff provenance (never `observed`); anything still absent stays null and listed in unresolved. Include a sample at cc/engine_handoff/example/requirements.granite.yaml with: handoff_id granite-b0-smoke-1, role inference-engine, model repository ibm-granite/granite-3.1-1b-a400m-instruct revision 0da7a48b0276d500ce5922fd2b33944091fc6c09, gpu nvidia x1, runtime compatibility \"CUDA runtime 12.8 (image nvidia/cuda:12.8.1-runtime); host driver >= 570\", limits cpus 8 memory 16g pids 512 timeout_s 300, network_after_staging none, tests requested [generation-smoke], policy_reference \"campaign decisions D005/D010 (ppl tripwire, paired KL)\", profiling requested false tool null (null allowed when requested=false).\n4. Tests (pytest, small synthetic docker-save fixtures built in the test with tarfile; do not require the 2.2 GB archive): classic layout, OCI layout, whiteout, tamper-in-layer rejection, handoff-edited-only rejection, requirements declared-vs-observed tagging, record/archive discrepancy surfaced.\n5. Run the real thing once and keep outputs: facts/generate/validate on the real b0 archive, writing to cc/engine_handoff/example-real/ (keep the run under ~3 minutes; report wall time). If validation is not `accepted`, list exactly what remains unresolved.\nNo network, no Docker. Time limit 40 min. Final message: files changed, test results, the real-run verdict + timing, open issues.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
